 "note": "The Dhātu-pāṭha, as a check on the roots this app carries and as the one source here that states a root's own sense in English. Only the roots lexicon/roots.json holds are extracted: nothing is fetched at build time, and the page must stay one self-contained file. `citation` is the form the Dhātu-pāṭha files the root under — often the Pāṇinian one (ṇam for nam, ṣṭhā for sthā) — and `hom` picks out which of its homonymous entries this is, so every claim is traceable back to a row. The curriculum stays canonical: where the two disagree the lesson wins and the build says so.",
